            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "qwkvet"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed this recipe exact except I doubled the rice. It was just what I expected and don't understand the negative comments at all. I also made a simple amaretto whip cream to top it with and loved it. It was a huge hit at my house and a family gathering (Italians lol). bake time for me was a little under 2 hours. The second time I made it I beat the eggs on high until they thickened, this made a much lighter, fluffier batter, for those who don't like the texture of traditional Ricotta pie give this a try.",
