            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "msatta"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is like the ricotta pie my mother in law makes (based on her Italian mother in laws recipe) but without crust and with rice. I would say this is more moist than ricotta pie. Made for Easter. My mother isn't big pineapple fan so I also went traditional and used the zest of 1 orange instead. I might add the juice also next time but it was so moist I doesn't really need it. I'll probably be eating for breakfast tomorrow. Nice that there is a low level of sugar overall, just tons of calories (but who's counting)",
